    {
      "id": 76,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -850,
        760
      ],
      "size": [
        1430,
        520
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.7",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# FLUX.2 Klein Base 9B: first image from text\n\n1. Put 'Required change: ...' and 'Result to show: ...' at the top of Positive prompt. Keep the general no-text instructions underneath.\n2. Confirm the three model files are selected, then queue the workflow.\n\nSettings: Euler, 20 steps, CFG 7, 1024 x 1024, seed 42 fixed. Width and Height feed both the scheduler and the output latent.\n\nImages must contain no words, letters, numbers, labels, captions, logos, or watermarks, including on packaging and interfaces. Keep written procedure details outside the image.\n\nThis canvas mirrors workflow_api.json, which the Python app uses for the first image. Later images use workflow_edit_api.json and edit the previous result with a fresh random seed. Use flux2_klein_9b_edit_workflow.json to test those edits manually.\n\nUpdate the API file too if you change this canvas manually; saving one format does not update the other. Model files and setup instructions are listed in README.md."
